---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import MistakeExhibits from '../../components/MistakeExhibits.astro'
import mistakes from '../../data/pytorch-mistakes.json'
---

<Base
  title="The mistake museum · the PyTorch wing — Rudrite Kernels"
  description="Six real PyTorch failures, reproduced and captured on CPU: the failing code, the exact error text, the fix, and the chapter that makes each impossible."
>
  <div class="ws-ground">
    <section class="wband">
      <div class="wrap wgrid">
        <span class="wtag">the museum<br />pytorch wing</span>
        <div>
          <p class="mono-label serves">serves the pytorch path · every error reproduced on this machine (torch 2.2.2, CPU, 2026-07-27), fixes run and proven · <a class="wing-link" href="/mistakes">all wings</a></p>
          <h1 class="wh1">The tape objects, in its own words.</h1>
          <p class="wlede">
            Six failures from the eager world, most of them autograd defending its tape: leaves
            mutated mid-graph, saved tensors rewritten, a graph walked twice. The snippet ran and
            failed; the error is verbatim (paths shortened); the fix ran and passed. The autograd
            chapter teaches the model that makes every one of these predictable.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <MistakeExhibits entries={mistakes} />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .serves { margin-bottom: 1rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .wing-link { color: var(--copper); text-decoration: none; }
  .wing-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
